  "worked_solution": "We're given the **rate of change** of volume $r(t).$ To find the total volume $V(t)$ after $t$ minutes, we apply the second fundamental theorem of calculus:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V(t) & =V(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{t}\\frac{15}{1+7{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =60+{\\int }_{0}^{t}\\frac{15}{1+7{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo ensure that our final function is a function of $t$ only, we use a different variable ($x$) for the integration.",
